title: Official Election Results — April 14, 1985
scene-id: election_results
is-card: true

= 1985 Peruvian Presidential Election Results

The official tally from the Jurado Nacional de Elecciones (JNE) confirms a decisive landslide:

+-------------------------------------------------------+
| PARTY / ALLIANCE                 | CANDIDATE | VOTES % |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
| APRA (Social Democracy)          | A. García | 53.1%   |
| Izquierda Unida (United Left)    | A. Barrantes| 24.7% |
| PPC (Popular Christian)          | L. Bedoya | 11.9%   |
| Acción Popular (Incumbent)       | J. Alva   |  7.3%   |
| Others / Null / Blank            | -         |  3.0%   |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

APRA has achieved an absolute majority in the first round. Outgoing President Fernando Belaúnde Terry contacts García to concede the race.

With a mandate from over half the electorate, the transition process begins immediately. Inauguration is set for July 28, 1985.

- @prep_transition: Begin presidential transition planning
